    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1965-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(z=0.363636\\ldots.\\) Then \\(100z-z=36,\\) so \\(z=\\frac{36}{99}=\\frac{4}{11}.\\) The requested sum is \\(4+11=15.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Multiply the decimal by \\(100\\) and subtract the original number",
        "Simplify \\(\\frac{36}{99}\\)"
      ],
